### Issue for this PR

Closes #59289

### Type of change

- [x] Bug fix

### What does this PR do?

Submitting a prompt while a turn is running called `session.switchAgent` eagerly. That publishes `agent.selected` immediately, the projector persists it, and the runner re-reads the agent at every step boundary — so the running turn got reconfigured mid-flight: new permissions, new tool snapshot, and the plan plugin told the model it was no longer restricted. Reproduced on 2.1.4 (V2, `dev`): a plan turn kept executing after the composer was flipped to build and the next prompt submitted, and it gained write access.

The fix carries the agent selection on the admitted prompt instead of applying it out of band. Admission queues a prompt whose agent differs from the session's, so an agent change can only ever land at a turn boundary. Promotion publishes `agent.selected` (with `previous`) right before the message becomes visible, and the runner re-takes its context selection when the persisted agent actually changed. The TUI and app composers pass the selection on the prompt rather than calling `switchAgent` first. Model switching behavior is untouched.

### How did you verify your code works?

- Two new runner scenarios: an agent-changing prompt queues while busy, the running turn keeps its agent, and the switch lands at the delivery boundary (`agent.selected` + `agent-switched` message); a selection matching the session agent still steers. Both fail on the pre-fix core (verified by stashing the source changes).
- Admission tests: differing agent queues, matching agent steers.
- Updated TUI transport and app composer tests for the new call pattern; schema contract suite passes; typecheck clean on schema, protocol, server, core, client, tui, app.

