## Bug

In pi-coding-agent **1.5.2**, the whole `pi` process crashes with an unhandled `AbortError` when a codemode script fails while a `read` tool call is still pending.

## Repro

One codemode script with parallel reads where one path does not exist:

```js
await Promise.all([
  tools.read({ path: "<some large existing file>" }),
  tools.read({ path: "./does-not-exist.md" }),
]);
```

The missing file rejects first, the script ends, `Execution.finish` aborts the pending tool calls, and the process exits:

```
AbortError: The operation was aborted
    at ReadStream.Readable (node:internal/streams/readable:354:7)
    at new ReadStream (node:internal/fs/streams:228:3)
    at FileHandle.createReadStream (node:internal/fs/promises:363:12)
    at Object.readLocalFileChunks [as createReadStream] (dist/bundle/chunks/chunk-VEJDBY3O.js:789)
    at async selectLinesFromStream (dist/bundle/chunks/chunk-VEJDBY3O.js:792)
Emitted 'error' event on ReadStream instance ...
  [cause]: DOMException [AbortError]
      at AbortController.abort
      at Execution.finish (dist/bundle/chunks/execute-L2EEDV3L.js:2)
```

Node v24.18.0, Linux x64. We hit it 3 times in one evening: agents often start by reading AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md in parallel, and the crash happens when one of them is missing.

## Cause

`readLocalFileChunks` creates the read stream with a signal that is already aborted. Node destroys the stream right away and emits `'error'`, but nothing is iterating the stream yet, so the error has no listener and takes down the process.

## Local fix we applied (works)

```js
async function* readLocalFileChunks(path, { signal }) {
  signal?.throwIfAborted();
  const handle = await fsOpen(path, "r");
  try {
    const stats = await handle.stat();
    const end = stats.isFile() && stats.size > 0 ? stats.size - 1 : undefined;
    signal?.throwIfAborted();
    const stream = handle.createReadStream({ end, signal, autoClose: false });
    stream.on("error", () => {}); // the iterator still sees the error; this only stops the crash
    yield* stream;
  } finally {
    await handle.close();
  }
}
```

With this patch the same script fails normally (`ENOENT` reported to the model) and the session keeps running.

## Summary
After a Feishu streaming card has been closed, the plugin keeps sending content updates to that card. The server rejects every one of them with `code=300309` (`streaming mode is closed`). The failures are not throttled or short-circuited, so they repeat for every subsequent partial reply and can span across turns, flooding the logs.

## Reproduction
1. Configure a Feishu account with `streaming.mode: "partial"`.
2. Exchange a few messages so that streaming cards are created and closed.
3. Inspect the gateway log for `Update card content failed` / `streaming mode is closed`.

Observed on one instance: 15 occurrences on 2026-11-14 and 223 occurrences on 2026-11-15, with a burst of roughly one per minute between 08:42 and 09:21. The rate is proportional to how often partial replies are produced, not to the number of cards.

## Cause
The CardKit write path does not record the terminal state returned by the server. When the server answers with `code=300309`, the failure is surfaced to the caller but no state is updated, so every later partial reply issues another identical update against the same already-closed card.

The write helper effectively behaves like:

```ts
try {
    await requestCardKit(`/${cardId}/elements/content${replace ? "" : "/content"}`, ...);
    return true;
} catch (error) {
    onError?.(error);   // <- no terminal state recorded
    return false;
}
```

and the update/flush paths only check `!this.state || this.closed`.

## Suggested fix
Treat `code=300309` as a terminal condition for that card: mark the session as closed by the server, drop any pending text, clear the flush timer, and short-circuit subsequent `update()` / `flushPendingUpdate()` calls. The final reply can still fall back to a normal (non-streaming) delivery.

```ts
} catch (error) {
    const message = error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error);
    if (message.includes("streaming mode is closed") || message.includes("300309")) {
        this.streamingClosedByServer = true;
        this.pendingText = null;
        this.clearFlushTimer();
    }
    onError?.(error);
    return false;
}
```

and in `update()` / `flushPendingUpdate()`:

```ts
if (!this.state || this.closed || this.streamingClosedByServer) return;
```

## Impact
Affected: Feishu channel with `streaming.mode: "partial"`. Causes log spam and wasted API calls against dead cards; each rejected write is a round trip to the Feishu API. Reported on OpenClaw `2026.11.3 (847611d)` with `@openclaw/feishu@2026.11.3`.

## Environment
- OpenClaw: 2026.11.3 (847611d)
- Plugin: @openclaw/feishu 2026.11.3
- Node: v26.13.1
- Channel: Feishu (open.feishu.cn)

